@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@adminUsername = admin
@adminPassword = change-this-before-testing
@staffUsername = staff.test
@staffPassword = change-this-staff-password
@csrfToken = paste-data.csrfToken-from-login-response-here

### Health is public
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### First-run check (public): hasUsers=false means the next registration becomes the administrator
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/status

### Register. On an empty users table this creates the administrator; afterwards it creates read-only staff.
### Registration also signs in: keep the Set-Cookie session and copy data.csrfToken into @csrfToken above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"{{adminUsername}}","fullName":"Desk Administrator","password":"{{adminPassword}}"}

### Duplicate username should return 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"{{adminUsername}}","password":"{{adminPassword}}"}

### Login (when the account already exists). Keep the Set-Cookie session and copy data.csrfToken into @csrfToken above.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"{{adminUsername}}","password":"{{adminPassword}}"}

### Authenticated session
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### Missing CSRF header should return 403 (no mutation is performed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/fruits
Content-Type: application/json

{"fruit_name":"CSRF check only","description":"This request must be rejected before writing.","status":"ACTIVE"}

### FAILING SALE — run against a fresh seed (Apples/LARGE = 6), before the purchase below
### The third line should return 409. Use scripts/demo-rollback.js to assert that stock and sale IDs stay unchanged.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sales
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"vendor_id":1,"items":[{"fruit_id":1,"packaging_size":"SMALL","quantity":2},{"fruit_id":2,"packaging_size":"SMALL","quantity":3},{"fruit_id":1,"packaging_size":"LARGE","quantity":10}]}

### Supplier endpoints
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/suppliers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/suppliers/1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/suppliers
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"business_name":"Test Orchard Supply","contact_person":"Mpho Test","phone":"+271199990001","province":"Gauteng","address":"Johannesburg market"}

### Duplicate phone should return 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/suppliers
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"business_name":"Duplicate Supplier","contact_person":"Test Contact","phone":"+271199990001","province":"Gauteng"}

### Update an existing supplier; deleting supplier 1 should return 409 because it has purchases
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/suppliers/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"business_name":"Highveld Harvest Co.","contact_person":"Thabo Mokoena","phone":"+27115550101","province":"Gauteng","address":"Johannesburg Fresh Produce Market"}
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/suppliers/1
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

### Supplier 8 has no seeded purchases; delete only in a disposable test database
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/suppliers/8
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

### Fruit endpoints
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/fruits
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/fruits
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"fruit_name":"Peaches","description":"Seasonal stone fruit","status":"ACTIVE"}
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/fruits/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"fruit_name":"Apples","description":"Crisp South African apples packed by size.","status":"ACTIVE"}

### Stock endpoints
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/stock
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/stock/fruit/1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/stock/low
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/stock/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"selling_price":35,"low_stock_threshold":10}

### Vendor endpoints
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/vendors
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/vendors/1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/vendors/search?q=market
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/vendors/1/balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/vendors/outstanding
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/vendors
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"vendor_name":"Test Maseru Retail","phone_number":"+26658119999","location":"Maseru Central"}
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/vendors/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"vendor_name":"Maseru Morning Market Stall","phone_number":"+26658110001","location":"Maseru Central Market"}

### Purchase transaction; this changes stock, so run after the failing-sale scenario
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/purchases
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"supplier_id":1,"items":[{"fruit_id":1,"packaging_size":"LARGE","quantity":1,"unit_cost":48},{"fruit_id":2,"packaging_size":"SMALL","quantity":5,"unit_cost":15}]}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/purchases
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/purchases/1

### Successful partially-paid sale; prices are looked up from stock by the server
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sales
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"vendor_id":1,"items":[{"fruit_id":2,"packaging_size":"SMALL","quantity":2}],"payment":{"amount":10,"method":"CASH"}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sales
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sales/1

### Payment endpoints: inspect seeded sale 2, record a valid payment, then confirm overpayment is rejected
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sales/2/payments
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sales/2/payments
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"amount":190,"method":"MOBILE_MONEY","reference":"TEST-MM-2"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/sales/2/payments
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"amount":0.01,"method":"CASH"}

### Reports: top 5 fruits, range revenue, trend chart, top vendor, stock levels
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reports/top-fruits
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reports/revenue?from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reports/revenue-trend?from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reports/top-vendor
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reports/stock-levels

### Team (administrator only): list accounts
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/users

### Promote a staff account (replace 2 with a user_id from the list); "staff" makes it read-only again.
### Demoting the only administrator returns 409.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/users/2/role
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

{"role":"admin"}

### Read-only staff check: register/login as staff in a separate client, then any POST/PUT/DELETE returns 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"{{staffUsername}}","password":"{{staffPassword}}"}

### Sign out after all authenticated requests
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}
